Assessment evidence

The performance/designs presented for assessment must be the student’s own work.

Students and teachers will be required to sign a Candidate record form (CRF) to fully authenticate
each student's work.

Programme notes

Teachers must provide programme notes for the moderator.

These must include photographs of each student so that each student is clearly identifiable to the
moderator.

The programme notes must also state each student’s chosen specialism.

In addition each student must offer a statement of their individual dramatic intentions to justify their
theatrical choices.

The Statement of Dramatic Intentions must be completed by the student on the template AQA
provides. This statement is not assessed directly but should be used to support assessment.
Assessment must not take place without reference to the student’s Statement of Dramatic
Intentions.

Recording

Assessed performances must be recorded with a single camera from an audience perspective
from start to finish and be unedited.

Each student being assessed must identify themselves by name and candidate number at the start
of the recording.

Students must also state their chosen specialism.

Close-ups of set, costume and puppet design students’ work must be included at the beginning of
the recording.

Full details of our requirements for recordings are provided at aqa.org.uk/drama

