  "definition": "A dramatic structure divided into four numbered acts, each advancing the central conflict towards an irreversible conclusion."
 },
 {
  "term": "lighting special",
  "definition": "A tightly focused area of illumination used to isolate a performer or object and draw audience attention."
 },
 {
  "term": "exposition",
  "definition": "The opening section of a play that introduces characters, setting, and the central conflict."
